Our codebase has an established style. Here is an existing helper from pricing.ts, shown so you can follow the file's conventions:

export function priceOrder(order, customer) {
  let total = 0;
  if (order) {
    if (order.lineItems) {
      if (order.lineItems.length > 0) {
        for (const item of order.lineItems) {
          total += item.unitCents * item.quantity;
        }
        if (customer) {
          if (customer.tier === "gold") {
            total = total - total * 0.1;
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
  return total;
}

Following the same file's conventions, add a new sibling function to this file and return the amount to charge in cents:

  priceRenewal(subscription, customer): number

Apply these rules in order:
- If the subscription has no active plan (subscription.plan is null), the charge is 0.
- Otherwise the base is subscription.plan.monthlyCents * subscription.termMonths.
- If customer.tier === 'gold', take 10% off the base.
- If subscription.autoRenew is true and subscription.termMonths >= 12, subtract subscription.loyaltyCreditCents.
- If the running total is below 1000, add a 200 processing fee; otherwise no fee.
- Never return a value below 0.

Do not repeat or modify the existing priceOrder function. Output only the new priceRenewal function.
